Tile by Tile (一片一片): credits

An unofficial fan film. Not made with, endorsed by or affiliated with Shenzhen Metro Group or any operator. No operator
logo, lettering or line bullet is used; line colours and station names are public facts.

Map data: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0. https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  Fetched 2026-11-13 through the Overpass API: the Shenzhen Metro route relations (network 深圳地铁) by neo/geo/routes.py into
  data/metro.json, the coastline and water areas by neo/geo/osm.py into data/coast.json, and both cut into a tile grid by
  tools/prep.py into data/mosaic.json. Those files are a derived database and stay under ODbL 1.0. The film is a produced
  work: it credits OpenStreetMap on the label of the mural (its last shot).
  View: 113.75-114.40 E, 22.45-22.85 N (lines that leave the box are kept whole), north up, equirectangular around
  114.075 E 22.65 N, one tile = 200 m. Only the coast, the sea, and lakes and reservoirs over 1.2 km² are drawn; long thin
  rivers are left out. No national, provincial or other boundary line is drawn: Shenzhen and Hong Kong are the same white
  tiles. Hong Kong's MTR lines are left out (they are not part of this story), by the network filter.
Facts on screen (opening dates, lengths, station totals): official and press sources listed in FACTS.md.

Picture: made entirely in code (three.js, physically based). No photographs, textures, video or 3D models are used;
  the station environment the glaze reflects is built in code.
Sound: the score (glass bells, porcelain tines, bass, glass harmonica), every sound effect and the station ambience are
  synthesized in numpy in mix.py. No samples or recordings are used.

Fonts (fetched by tools/fonts.sh into fonts/, not kept in git):
- Source Han Sans CN, Bold and Heavy. Adobe. SIL Open Font License 1.1.
  https://github.com/adobe-fonts/source-han-sans (tag 2.004R)
- Barlow Semi Condensed, Medium and SemiBold. Jeremy Tribby. SIL Open Font License 1.1.
  https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/barlowsemicondensed

Tools: the NEO-Cine library's core/ tools, which are Lemo-Opuscar's (MIT, (c) 2026 LemoLab): headless Chrome frame
capture, ffmpeg encode and loudness master; three.js r170 (MIT).

Form reference (grammar only, none of their designs or lettering are used): hand-set station wall mosaics, opus
vermiculatum, vitreous-enamel signs.

The wall is an illustration, not a survey: each line is a chain of tiles one tile apart along its OpenStreetMap path;
where two lines share a corridor, the later one is set one tile aside.
